course: dictionary
lesson: 10477
title: One word, many tunes
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, so you need the context to know which one is right. «The orchestra players tune up before they play.» Here tune means to adjust their instruments so the notes are right, not a song.
explain: «The little girl hummed a tune she had learned at school.» You can hum a tune because it is a series of notes that makes a song you can remember. Try swapping your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
explain: «Her singing was out of tune, so the teacher asked her to listen again.» Out of tune means the notes are wrong. Tune can also mean setting a radio or TV to a channel: «Stay tuned, because the show is about to start» means keep watching.
explain: «"Alouette, gentille alouette" is a cheerful tune, but its words are about plucking a lark's feathers.» Some tunes sound happier than their words. Listening hard, then copying the tune, is how you get it right.
fact: Tune can be a noun (a tune) or a verb (to tune, tuned, tuning).
fact: «A tune» is a series of musical notes that makes a song or melody you can remember and hum.
fact: «To tune» an instrument means to adjust it so its notes are at the right pitch.
fact: «In tune» means singing or playing the right notes; «out of tune» means the notes are wrong.
fact: «Tune in» means switch on to watch or listen, and «stay tuned» means keep watching.
exercise: «In music lessons, pupils learn tunes and sing them.» What is a tune? | A loud noise in a classroom | *A series of musical notes that makes a song you can remember and hum | A type of drum | A word for a bad singer
exercise: «The orchestra players tune up before they play.» What does tune up mean here? | Leave the stage to get a drink | *Adjust their instruments so the notes are at the right pitch | Go to sleep before the concert | Sing as loudly as they can
exercise: «Stay tuned for the next episode!» What does stay tuned mean? | Stand still and wait for a bus | Sing a song quietly | Turn off the TV | *Keep watching or listening
test: «He played a wrong note, and the singing went out of tune.» What does out of tune mean? | *The notes are wrong | Very loud | Happy and bright | Finished
test: «"Alouette, gentille alouette" is a cheerful tune about plucking a lark's feathers.» Find and copy one word that means happy and bright. | feathers | lark | *cheerful | plucking
exam: Which phrase means switch on to watch or listen? | out of tune | *tune in | change your tune | to the tune of
